// XFAIL: RT-393: (RT-393's mechanism, a blanket impl over it) `impl Tr for W where W: Conv` with no impl of Conv for W meets the blanket `impl<T: Tr> Q for T`, and `w.q()` runs and prints 9: code runs whose bound fails (rustc E0277 at the impl, E0599 at the call) (0.30.2)
// From the review of g302oblig-m2 (form f269al). Since v0.30.1 at least;
// the release build the same. rustc E0277 (`W: Conv` is not satisfied)
// at the impl's where clause and E0599 (the method `q` exists, but its
// trait bounds were not satisfied) at the call (the rustc twin of this
// file). Siblings: rt_393, rt_393b, rt_393d.
// ERROR: line 25
// ERROR: line 39
trait Conv {
    fn c(&self) -> i64;
}

trait Tr {
    fn f(&self) -> i64;
}

trait Q {
    fn q(&self) -> i64;
}

struct W {
    r: i64,
}

impl Tr for W where W: Conv {
    fn f(&self) -> i64 {
        1
    }
}

impl<T: Tr> Q for T {
    fn q(&self) -> i64 {
        9
    }
}

fn main() {
    let w = W { r: 0 };
    println("{}", w.q());
}
